<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Fuller parts lists for Close Air Support's A-10 and Su-25 (owner, 21 Nov 2026: the Harrier's treatment;
    docs/development/close-air-support-jets.md). Each jet keeps its own five parts (airframe, armoured cockpit, two engines, the
    self-sealing tanks) with their keys, health and order: Vehicle Framework saves a vehicle's parts by position, so new ones are only
    ever appended, and D'thorga Framework gives a saved jet the new parts at full health when it loads.

    Six parts each, fewer than the Harrier's ten on purpose: the jets' own rule moves a share of hits onto a part other than the airframe,
    chosen evenly among every part with cells of its own (their HitSpread, read 21 Nov 2026, the Harrier's rule), so every part added
    takes hits away from the cockpit and the engines. Neither jet carries a radar, so none is added; their exhausts and intakes are part of
    their engines. What each does: avionics, hydraulics and wiring carry flight control, which D'thorga Framework's rule turns into slower
    flight and, below 35 %, a refused take-off; the landing gear carries move speed on the ground; the pylons and the gun take hits and
    need repair. The hydraulics part stands for both of each jet's two independent systems (a simplification). Health, armour and cells
    are authored, scaled to each jet's own parts (the Su-25's about 85 % of the A-10's, as its author scaled them). Cells are the jet's own,
    facing north: x across, z along, the nose at the top.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="Warthog_Jet"]/components</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>
        <key>PhobosAvionics</key>
        <label>avionics</label>
        <health>50</health>
        <depth>Internal</depth>
        <armor>
          <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.25</ArmorRating_Blunt>
          <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.50</ArmorRating_Sharp>
        </armor>
        <hitbox>
          <cells>
            <li>(0, 3)</li>
          </cells>
        </hitbox>
        <categories>
          <li>FlightControl</li>
        </categories>
      </li>
      <li>
        <key>PhobosHydraulics</key>
        <label>hydraulics</label>
        <health>60</health>
        <depth>Internal</depth>
        <armor>
